{
  "number": 2173,
  "title": "[BUG] SlidingWindowConversationManager.reduce_context fails to trim tool-heavy conversations after v1.35.0",
  "url": "https://github.com/strands-agents/harness-sdk/issues/2173",
  "state": "closed",
  "created_at": "2026-04-21T05:32:23Z",
  "closed_at": "2026-04-22T18:05:46Z",
  "body": "### Checks\n\n- [x] I have updated to the lastest minor and patch version of Strands\n- [x] I have checked the documentation and this is not expected behavior\n- [x] I have searched [./issues](./issues?q=) and there are no duplicates of my issue\n\n### Strands Version\n\n1.35.0\n\n### Python Version\n\n3.11\n\n### Operating System\n\nLinux\n\n### Installation Method\n\npip\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n\n```\nfrom strands.agent.conversation_manager import SlidingWindowConversationManager\nfrom strands.types.exceptions import ContextWindowOverflowException\nfrom unittest.mock import MagicMock\n\nmanager = SlidingWindowConversationManager(window_size=4)\n\nagent = MagicMock()\nagent.messages = [\n    {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": [{\"text\": \"Review this PR\"}]},\n    {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": [{\"toolUse\": {\"toolUseId\": \"1\", \"name\": \"get_diff\", \"input\": {}}}]},\n    {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": [{\"toolResult\": {\"toolUseId\": \"1\", \"content\": [{\"text\": \"diff data\"}], \"status\": \"success\"}}]},\n    {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": [{\"toolUse\": {\"toolUseId\": \"2\", \"name\": \"get_file\", \"input\": {}}}]},\n    {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": [{\"toolResult\": {\"toolUseId\": \"2\", \"content\": [{\"text\": \"file data\"}], \"status\": \"success\"}}]},\n    {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": [{\"toolUse\": {\"toolUseId\": \"3\", \"name\": \"get_tree\", \"input\": {}}}]},\n    {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": [{\"toolResult\": {\"toolUseId\": \"3\", \"content\": [{\"text\": \"tree data\"}], \"status\": \"success\"}}]},\n    {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": [{\"text\": \"Here is my review\"}]},\n]\n\nmanager.reduce_context(agent, e=Exception(\"context window overflow\"))\n```\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\nreduce_context should successfully trim the conversation, as it did in v1.34.1 (which trims to 3 messages for this input).\n\n### Actual Behavior\n\nreduce_context raises ContextWindowOverflowException: Unable to trim conversation context!\n\nThe user-first enforcement added in PR#2087 skips all assistant messages as trim points. Combined with the existing toolResult check that skips user messages containing tool results, there are no valid trim points in tool-heavy conversations:\n\nuser (prompt)           ← only plain user message, but before trim window\nassistant (tool call)   ← skipped: not a user message\nuser (tool result)      ← skipped: contains toolResult\nassistant (tool call)   ← skipped: not a user message\nuser (tool result)      ← skipped: contains toolResult\nassistant (tool call)   ← skipped: not a user message\nuser (tool result)      ← skipped: contains toolResult\nassistant (response)    ← skipped: not a user message\n\n### Additional Context\n\n_No response_\n\n### Possible Solution\n\nWhen no plain user message exists within the trim range, fall back to trimming at an assistant(toolUse) + user(toolResult) boundary. This preserves the user-first fix for providers like Bedrock Nova (no bare assistant messages) while still allowing trimming in tool-heavy conversations. The conversation would start with a valid complete tool interaction pair.\n\n### Related Issues\n\nhttps://github.com/strands-agents/sdk-python/issues/2085",
